==Trivia==
* During Tiger's transformation, the user will gain a moderate speed boost/buff. Using [[Rabbit V3]] and the [[Pilot Helmet]] adds even more speed buffs. Combining all of them can make the user surpass the speed of Awakened [[Light]]'s {{Ability|Light|F|2}} (the second fastest flight).
** This move can also be added onto the transformation combination to make it even faster.
* The fruit takes heavy design inspiration from the Kung Fu Panda antagonist, Tai Lung.
* Tiger's M1 attacks can damage [[Sea Beast]]s.
* Strangely, using transformed (Blazing Form) {{Ability|X}} to a transformed [[Dragon]], they can "push" the Dragon away briefly.
* Tiger is widely considered a ''spammable'' fruit. Using the combination of [[Zebra Cap]], [[Ghoul]] V3/V4 - which has the ability to reduce cooldowns - and its '''Blazing Form''' will massively contribute to the fruit's cooldown reduction, or ''spammability'', so much that if used properly, the player can almost use the moves continuously.
* [[Yeti]] and Tiger are the second pair of fruits to share the same price, the first being [[Mammoth]] and [[T-Rex]].
* Tiger is the first fruit to have a [[Mutations|mutation]] in Blox Fruits, being [[Werewolf]].
* Tiger is the second fruit that has 2 transformations, the first one being [[Dragon]].
* [[Yeti]] is considered to be the rival of Leopard as shown in their respective rework/release trailers, and both [[Yeti]] and Tiger stand as the pinnacle for non-fury-meter [[Beast]] fruits.
* Despite the '''[Z]''' move being called '''''Finger'' Revolver''', the animation is more resemblant to punching.
** This is likely due to the name not being changed from [[Leopard]], since it indeed had animations for finger movement.
* When using the M1's (with enough lag) while transformed, there's a chance that the user will be abruptly teleported to the [[sea]] and then be teleported back right after.
** Sometimes, the user will be abruptly teleported to a nearby location after briefly teleporting to the [[sea]], rather than their exact position prior to the glitch happening. When at [[Castle on the Sea]], [[Hydra Island]], or near [[Mansion (Third Sea)|Mansion]], the user may be teleported to the [[Third Sea]] [[portals]], causing them to go back and forth between islands if they have access.
** There is also a very rare chance the user will not be teleported back and will be stranded at [[sea]].
* {{Ability|X}} can fling objects on the ground.
* After using {{Ability|V}} before the fire meter is full will take the user back to base form and completely deplete the fire meter.
* Tiger now allows for the newest, highest potential speed on ground for a player in the game by combining the following: Blazing Form + 
Afterimage Assault + [[Rabbit#Version 4|Rabbit V4]] (and [[Agility]]) + [[Pilot Helmet]]. However, this is still not the fastest transportation method, as [[Portal]] has the ability to almost instantly teleport to most [[locations|islands]] in any sea.

